-- title:
--   Depth equals Krull dimension for 𝒪[[X₁,…,Xₙ]]
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, let $n$ be a natural number, and write $\Lambda =$ `MvPowerSeries (Fin n) 𝓞` for the ring of formal power series over $\mathcal{O}$ in the variables indexed by `Fin n`. The assertion is an equality in `WithBot ℕ∞` between two invariants of $\Lambda$. On the left is the depth of $\Lambda$ as a module over itself, in the sense of the project notion [`Module.depth`](def/Patching_SystemTypes.html#L34): the supremum, in $\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$, of the lengths of those finite lists $s$ of elements of $\Lambda$ which form a weakly regular sequence on the module $\Lambda$ and all of whose entries lie in the maximal ideal of the local ring $\Lambda$; this supremum is then coerced into `WithBot ℕ∞`. On the right is the Krull dimension `ringKrullDim` of $\Lambda$, the supremum of lengths of chains of prime ideals, taken in `WithBot ℕ∞` so that the empty-spectrum case has a value. No further hypotheses are imposed; in particular $n = 0$ is allowed, the statement then reading $\operatorname{depth}_{\mathcal{O}}\mathcal{O} = \dim \mathcal{O}$.
--
--   This is the Cohen–Macaulay property of the regular local ring $\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$, whose common value of depth and dimension is $n+1$. It supplies the equality of depth and Krull dimension that the patching argument requires of the ring $S_\infty$ when deducing, via the Auslander–Buchsbaum formula, that the patched module is free; it is used here in the freeness and rank computation for quotients of a formal group by the ideal generated by a sequence of power series.
-- source:
